<h1>Flim Summaries — terms of use</h1>
<p class="lede-inline">
  These terms apply to the optional Flim Summaries service. The main app has
  separate
  <a href="/acceptable-use">terms</a>.
</p>
<p>Last updated: 18 October 2026.</p>

<h2>What you get</h2>
<p>
  Flim Summaries can turn a voice message into a title, a short summary, and a
  transcript when you choose Flim’s option in the app. You need a Flim Summaries
  account with remaining allowance on a plan (or a promo).
</p>

<h2>Account</h2>
<p>
  Sign-in uses an email address and a one-time code. You’re responsible for the
  email you use and for keeping access to it. Don’t share sign-in codes.
</p>

<h2>Plans, allowance, and promos</h2>
<p>
  Usage is limited by the plan or promo attached to your account. When allowance
  runs out, new summaries fail until it renews or you change plan. Promo terms
  may add extra limits.
</p>

<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
<p>
  Use the service for your own chats in good faith. Don’t try to bypass rate
  limits or allowance, don’t hammer the API, and don’t use it for harassment,
  scams, or anything illegal. Audio longer than <strong>30 minutes</strong> for
  a single voice message is refused.
</p>

<h2>No warranty</h2>
<p>
  Titles and summaries are machine-generated and can be wrong or incomplete.
  The service is provided as-is; availability and quality are not guaranteed.
</p>

<h2>Suspension</h2>
<p>
  We may suspend or close accounts that abuse the service, bypass limits, or
  break these terms.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>
  We may change these terms as the service changes. We’ll publish the updated
  terms here and update the date above. If you keep using Flim Summaries after a
  change takes effect, the updated terms apply.
</p>

